  "query_preview": "../Friday through Tuesday-written Tuesday/... The \nridge of high pressure in the Gulf of Alaska looks to begin to \nbreak down into the weekend. Overall, the weather pattern still \nlooks fairly benign, but there could be some convective showers \nforming in British Columbia with easterly flow aloft Saturday. \nRight now, instability in the Alaska Panhandle looks quite low, so\nthis should limit chances of this activity approaching Southeast \nAlaska. \n\n With model discrepancies this far out, there is still uncertainty \nas to where the best chances for precipitation will set-up. Any \nprecipitation that does form looks to have fairly low accumulations \nfor the area (less than 0.5\").",
